{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of PostHog’s batch capture API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/batch\/"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogBatchEncoder"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and PostHog’s limits:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com","    plan: plan)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":" with two members: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"api_key"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"project token, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"type":"text","text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, by name, then the members listed below"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked: ISO 8601 in UTC, with milliseconds ("},{"code":"2026-11-23T14:03:27.512Z","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent, and every event is anonymous: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"text":" holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"text":", so PostHog makes no person profile, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so PostHog doesn’t add a location from the request’s IP address. A record with no session (one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"text":") is its own anonymous person, linked to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing: PostHog rejects a whole batch when one of its events has no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":". A record a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"text":" of its first send. PostHog counts a person per ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":", so its unique users","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are sessions. The session is also sent as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"text":", which PostHog’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions and web analytics group events by (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":" is the UUIDv7 they require); a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with no session has none. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property whose name starts with ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which only a hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write, or is ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is left out and logged at notice level, as PostHog reads those","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names as settings (","type":"text"},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or the identity.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_namespace"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle identifier, version and build, each left out when "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_model"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_type"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mobile"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tablet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Desktop"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TV"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vision"},{"type":"text","text":" for the form factor; no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_type"},{"type":"text","text":" for a watch"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$locale","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$network_wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$network_cellular","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi, and whether it is cellular","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a name PostHog keeps for its own events), one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for PostHog to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. PostHog answers a batch it takes with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"200, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","t